.TH WB\-CHECK 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-check \- say whether the repository is at its revision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR check
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Say whether the repository still is at the revision it is pinned to: each file under .watchbill/revision/ against the manifest, the manifest against the revision line of watchbill.yml, and that revision against the installed wb, and the project text for a placeholder the revision does not know.
.PP
It writes nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All of it holds.
.TP
.B 1
Something differs.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wb (1) ,
.BR wb\-init (1) ,
.BR wb\-upgrade (1)
